  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The government submitted the reports in a timely manner on 31 August 2022 on Conventions 29,105,138, and 182.   The Government submitted the reports for  Conventions 88, 100, and 111 and the out-of-cycle reports for C 98 and MLC before 1 September 2023. The ILO provided technical support in terms of assisting the Government to clarify the comments made by the supervisory bodies. In 2023, Indonesia was called upon to provide information to the CAS on measures taken or considered to improve the application of C 98. The ILO assisted the Government by providing technical expertise and facilitated a workshop for the preparation of the report on C 98 in August 2023, with RBSA funding.</narrative>
   </description>
