  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of Member States to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The new members of the National Tripartite Council 2023- 206 were inaugurated by the Government in July 2023.  The agenda of the National Tripartite Council includes providing recommendations to the Government on the implementation of international labour standards and national policies related to labour and employment. During the previous period 2021-2023, the National Tripartite discussed matter related to inputs to the employment creation law, wages during the covid-19 pandemic, protection for gig economy workers, etc. In addition to the National tripartite Council, in certain circumstances, the Government organized ad-hoc tripartite meetings inviting social partners beyond the members of the National Tripartite Council, such as for issues related to domestic workers, sectoral issues such as fishing and palm oil, and prevention of sexual harassment at the workplace. With RBSA funding, the ILO provided facilitation for organizing tripartite meetings and consultation to ensure effective engagement of the social partners in the implementation of the international labour standards such as conventions 188, 29, 105, 81, and 144.</narrative>
   </description>
